So how do you test, for example, whether ESP exists? With respect to testing ESP, there are a number of established ways of doing it, One technique which I've never actually used personally, but one which is still something of a challenge for skeptics to explain away. I'm not convinced overall, otherwise I wouldn't be a skeptic. But the so-called Gansfeldt technique, this is based on the idea that if there is such a thing as ESP, then it's maybe a very weak signal, which is usually kind of drowned out by all the other processing that's going on in our brains at the time. Now, if there's anything in that idea, the things to do would be to try and dampen down the background activity so that the ESP signal, the telepathy signal, can come through. So what people do is you get a sender and a receiver, two people taking part in the study.
那么，你如何检验例如ESP（超感官知觉）是否存在呢？关于检验ESP，有许多既定的方法。有一种技术我个人实际上从未使用过，但它仍然是怀疑论者难以解释清楚的一个挑战。总的来说我并不确信，否则我就不会成为一个怀疑论者了。但所谓的“甘斯菲尔德技术”（Ganzfeld technique），其背后的想法是：如果真的存在ESP这种东西，那么它可能是一个非常微弱的信号，通常会被我们大脑中当时正在进行的所有其他处理过程所淹没。现在，如果这个观点有任何道理，那么要做的事情就是试图减弱背景活动，以便ESP信号、心灵感应信号能够穿透进来。所以人们的做法是找一个发送者和接收者，两个人参与研究。

