could you just describe that a little bit more clearly, just to get all clarified and all recorded. But the clincher is when either the receiver or independent judges say what is the best match from the four available video clips to the imagery that the person was describing. Now, you would expect by chance people to get a hit rate of 25%, but it was claimed that people were getting hit rates of more like 33%. So not a massive effect, but statistically significant. That's one example.
“你能把那个描述得更清楚一点吗？”只是为了把所有内容都澄清并记录下来。但决定性的关键在于，当接收者或独立评判者指出，在四个可用的视频片段中，哪一个与此人所描述的意象最匹配。现在，按照偶然概率，人们的命中率应该为25%，但据称人们的命中率更接近于33%。所以这不是一个巨大的效应，但在统计学上是显著的。这是一个例子。

